<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>A Step-by-Step Guide to Implementing Supply Chain Management</b></h3>
                <p>A supply chain management solution can connect suppliers, procurement, inventory, production, logistics, and operational workflows to improve visibility and coordination across the supply chain.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Supply Chain Strategy Planning: Identify supplier, procurement, inventory, production, logistics, demand, and reporting requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Centralized Supply Chain Data: Organize supplier, purchase, inventory, logistics, and operational information in a structured platform.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Supply Chain Workflow Automation: Automate approvals, purchase workflows, supplier notifications, alerts, and routine supply chain tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Secure Access: Apply role-based access controls to protect supplier and business information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Continuous Supply Chain Optimization: Use analytics, performance data, and feedback to improve supply chain processes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>Key Critical Factors for a Successful Supply Chain Management Solution</b></h3>
                <p>Supply chain management requires strong coordination across procurement, suppliers, inventory, production, logistics, data, and reporting.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Clear Supply Chain Objectives: Define measurable goals for lead times, supplier performance, inventory availability, procurement efficiency, and delivery.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Quality Supplier Data: Maintain accurate supplier, purchasing, product, delivery, and performance information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Workflow Automation: Automate purchase approvals, supplier communication, alerts, and routine activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  End-to-End Visibility: Connect procurement, inventory, production, and logistics information for better coordination.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  User Adoption: Provide intuitive workflows and training for procurement and supply chain teams.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Supply Chain Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Supply Chain Management" /></div>
