<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Managing Change for Successful Supply Chain Management Adoption</b></h3>
                <p>Supply chain transformation affects multiple teams and external relationships. A structured adoption strategy helps users consistently follow new workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Explain the Supply Chain Vision: Communicate how connected workflows improve visibility, coordination, and efficiency.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Engage Stakeholders: Involve procurement, suppliers, warehouse, production, finance, logistics, and management teams.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Role-Based Training: Train users on supply chain functions relevant to their roles.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Roll Out in Phases: Introduce capabilities progressively and monitor adoption.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Ongoing Support: Address user questions and continuously optimize supply chain processes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>How to Optimize Supply Chain Management for Maximum ROI</b></h3>
                <p>A connected supply chain solution should continuously improve procurement efficiency, supplier performance, inventory availability, and delivery outcomes.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Define Supply Chain KPIs: Measure supplier performance, lead times, purchase cycle time, stock availability, and delivery performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Integrate Core Systems: Connect supply chain with procurement, inventory, production, ERP, and logistics applications.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Improve User Experience: Simplify purchasing, approvals, supplier tracking, and operational workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Review Supply Chain Performance: Regularly assess suppliers, lead times, workflows, and business outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Leverage Automation and Analytics: Use automation and analytics to improve supplier and supply chain decisions.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Supply Chain Management" /></div>
